{"name":"Turning Oakleaf","hex":"#ede1a8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A turn or deviation from a straight course.","At hockey, a foul committed by a player attempting to hit the ball who interposes their body between the ball and an opposing player trying to do the same."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of turn"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turning"},{"term":"oakleaf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The leaf of an oak tree.","A device, badge or emblem shaped like the leaf of an oak, and indicating an award."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oakleaf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turning","blocks":[{"text":"Turning is a machining process in which a cutting tool is held nearly stationary to cut a rotating workpiece. The cutting tool can be slowly moved back-and-forth and in-and-out to cut cylindrical shapes and flat surfaces on the workpiece. Turning is usually done with a lathe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/SchruppenDrehen.jpg/330px-SchruppenDrehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turning"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/StechenDrehen.jpg/500px-StechenDrehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/StechenDrehen.jpg/500px-StechenDrehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parting aluminium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStechenDrehen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/SchlichtenDrehen.jpg/500px-SchlichtenDrehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/S